 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Cash rate:** The RBA cash rate target has risen by 4.26 percentage points since January 2022, from 0.10% (monthly average for January 2022) to 4.36% (monthly average for September 2026, the latest data). Most of the rise came in 2022 and 2023, when it went from 0.10% to 4.35% by the end of 2023. It was then held at 4.35% through 2024 and most of 2025. The RBA cut it to 3.60% by late 2025, then lifted it back to 4.35% in June 2026 and 4.36% in September 2026.\n\n**Sydney rents:** Rent growth is 3.5% over the year to August 2026 (ABS CPI, original series). That is down from 5.6% in January 2025, but it has been fairly steady at 3.3–3.5% since January 2026. For comparison, national rent growth was 3.6% in August 2026.",
